{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"c2ebf2f8be4f385ce268a895cee811cb5f67eda1b3e429169c11e509cdaf57b3","digest":{"component_or_area":"store initialization and marker management","key_entities":["*/.archived","*/.write.lock","rebar._store.ensures.REGISTRY_IDS","rebar._commands.init","reducer/_api.py","reducer/marker.py","untrack-runtime-markers","git ls-files","git rm --cached"],"problem_keywords":["tracked runtime markers","gitignore","git status","plan review","marker cache","archive","self-healing"],"propositions":["Runtime marker files (*/.archived, */.write.lock) are tracked in the tickets branch but should be untracked because they are derived local caches, causing dirty git status and breaking plan-review attestations.","An ensure unit untrack-runtime-markers removes tracked marker files from git index via batched git rm --cached with a single commit, leaving worktree copies intact.","Peers merging the untrack commit have tracked marker copies deleted by git, and the reader self-heals by re-materializing missing .archived markers for archived tickets in the list path.","The self-healing mechanism in reducer/_api.py mirrors the existing stale-marker-clearing behavior and applies only to exclude_archived lists to avoid materializing markers unnecessarily."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787763986533164001,"uuid":"063504a0-6e9d-495d-99cd-2e61bd6ded57"}